      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NUNYA (2) placed on debut across the Tasman last November then transferred to the Bain/Taylor stable at Murray Bridge. Failed at the only Australian run in April and was put away. Going well in preparation for this - expecting a lot more today. PRETTY MORSEL (6) has been in the money five runs in a row, and nine from 16 overall. Closed strongly to get up for second last start over this distance at Balaklava. Starting to form a habit but in this company she gets her chance to break through. EMBERANCE (4) started at $101 but finished hard and was only beaten 1.5 lengths first-up over 1300m at Balaklava. Might have turned the corner and over a slightly longer trip looks a strong contender. ROAD TO THE CITY (3) led but found a couple better over this distance at Balaklava last start, the fifth minor placing from 19 runs. Each-way hope again. INTIMUS (9) was strong through the line over 1200m last time and should relish stepping up in journey.",
